\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. For all the saints who from their labours rest
\par Who Thee by faith before the world confessed,
\par Thy name, O Jesu, be for ever blest,
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou their Rock, their Fortress, and their Might;
\par Thou, Lord, their Captain in the well fought fight;
\par Thou in the darkness drear their one true Light.
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O may Thy soldiers, faithful, true, and bold,
\par Fight as the saints who nobly fought of old,
\par And win, with them, the victor's crown of gold!
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O blest communion, fellowship divine!
\par We feebly struggle; they in glory shine,
\par Yet all are one in Thee, for all are Thine.
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And when the strife is fierce, the warfare long,
\par Steals on the ear the distant triumph song,
\par And hearts are brave again, and arms are strong.
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The golden evening brightens in the west;
\par Soon, soon to faithful warriors cometh rest;
\par Sweet is the cam of paradise the best.
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. But lo! there breaks a yet more glorious day:
\par The saints triumphant rise in bright array;
\par The King of Glory passes on His way!
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. From earth's wide bounds, from ocean's farthest coast,
\par Through gates of pearl streams in the countless host,
\par Singing to Father, Son, and Holy Ghost:
\par Alleluia!
\par 
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

